'''Parc Sakura''' ({{Literal translation|Sakura Park}}) is a [[W:Public park|public park]] located in the [[Nueva Cuenca]] neighborhood in [[Hisbanya]], [[Castejón]], directly north of the [[Tidal Basin (Hisbanya)|Tidal Basin]]. In 1893, the [[Baliscan-Sanese Friendship Committee]] of Castejón donated 2,500 cherry blossom trees to the city, to commemorate the 25th anniversary of the [[Balisca-Okaiken relations|establishment of diplomatic relations]]. The famous [[W:Sakura|sakura]] cherry trees of the park are the main attraction at the [[Cherry Blossom Festival (Balisca)|Metropolitan Cherry Blossom Festival]] (popularly known by the [[Sanese language|Sanese]] term ''[[W:Hanami|Hanami]]''; {{Literal translation|flower viewing}}) in early spring, when the cherry blossoms bloom. 

